          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پادشاه (pâdeshâh) — \"a king, a monarch\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پادشاه (pâdeshâh) سه پسر داشت. Pâdeshâh se pesar dâsht. The king had three sons."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also shâh. Pâdeshâhi \"a kingdom, a reign\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pâdeshâh is a native Persian word that EtymDB glosses \"king, monarch\" without a parent; it is usually traced to Middle Persian pādixšāh, \"ruler\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
